  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "(c) We note that\n$\\frac{d}{d x}(x \\tan x+1)=x \\sec ^2 x+\\tan x$\n$\\therefore$ integrating by parts with $x^2$ as first function, we get\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& I=\\int x^2 \\frac{x \\sec ^2 x+\\tan x}{(x \\tan x+1)^2} d x \\\\\n& =x^2\\left(-\\frac{1}{x \\tan x+1}\\right)-\\int 2 x\\left(-\\frac{1}{x \\tan x+1}\\right) d x \\\\\n& =-\\frac{x^2}{x \\tan x+1}+2 \\int \\frac{x \\cos x}{x \\sin x+\\cos x} d x \\\\\n& =-\\frac{x^2}{x \\tan x+1}+2 \\log _e|x \\sin x+\\cos x|+c \\\\\n& \\quad\\left(\\because \\frac{d}{d x}(x \\sin x+\\cos x)=x \\cos x\\right)\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
